vendor/cros-libva: cros-libva 0.0.12 (crates.io, BSD-3-Clause), with fixes: src/buffer/vp9.rs so it builds against libva 2.23+; Display::create_context never makes a context smaller than the driver's minimum surface size (cros-codecs opens every decoder with a 16x16 context, which radeonsi and nvidia-vaapi-driver refuse); Display::open_drm_display_with_driver picks the VA driver (vaSetDriverName) instead of LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME, which applies to every device. The bindings are pregenerated in src/bindings_generated.rs, so a build needs no bindgen/clang: they are the OUT_DIR/bindings.rs the crate's original build.rs (with bindgen_gen.rs and libva-wrapper.h from the crates.io package) generates from libva 2.24 headers; identical for x86_64 and aarch64. To update them, run that original build.rs against newer headers and copy the file over
vendor/re_mp4: re_mp4 0.4.0 (crates.io, MIT/Apache-2.0), unknown metadata data-atom types become Binary and odd audio track fields fall back to defaults instead of failing the whole file
